   <conbody class="- topic/body  concept/conbody " xtrf="file:/C:/Users/adity/Downloads/Analytics%20User%20Guide/output/motor_object/overview_3.dita" xtrc="conbody:1;25:13">
      <p class="- topic/p " xtrf="file:/C:/Users/adity/Downloads/Analytics%20User%20Guide/output/motor_object/overview_3.dita" xtrc="p:1;26:10">The motor object consists of a components map. Each component has a Fault Score Index (FSI) and a Code. The FSI is a value between 0 and 10, which indicates the following motor conditions or state:</p>
      <ul id="ul_10211553" class="- topic/ul " xtrf="file:/C:/Users/adity/Downloads/Analytics%20User%20Guide/output/motor_object/overview_3.dita" xtrc="ul:1;27:28">
         <li class="- topic/li " xtrf="file:/C:/Users/adity/Downloads/Analytics%20User%20Guide/output/motor_object/overview_3.dita" xtrc="li:1;28:14">FSI &lt; ‘5ʼ: <b class="+ topic/ph hi-d/b " xtrf="file:/C:/Users/adity/Downloads/Analytics%20User%20Guide/output/motor_object/overview_3.dita" xtrc="b:1;28:31">Alarm</b>
         </li>
         <li class="- topic/li " xtrf="file:/C:/Users/adity/Downloads/Analytics%20User%20Guide/output/motor_object/overview_3.dita" xtrc="li:2;30:14">FSI= ‘5ʼ or ‘6ʼ: <b class="+ topic/ph hi-d/b " xtrf="file:/C:/Users/adity/Downloads/Analytics%20User%20Guide/output/motor_object/overview_3.dita" xtrc="b:2;30:34">Warning</b>
         </li>
         <li class="- topic/li " xtrf="file:/C:/Users/adity/Downloads/Analytics%20User%20Guide/output/motor_object/overview_3.dita" xtrc="li:3;32:14">FSI &gt; ‘6ʼ: <b class="+ topic/ph hi-d/b " xtrf="file:/C:/Users/adity/Downloads/Analytics%20User%20Guide/output/motor_object/overview_3.dita" xtrc="b:3;32:31">Good</b>.</li>
      </ul>
      <note type="note" class="- topic/note " xtrf="file:/C:/Users/adity/Downloads/Analytics%20User%20Guide/output/motor_object/overview_3.dita" xtrc="note:1;34:25">
         <b class="+ topic/ph hi-d/b " xtrf="file:/C:/Users/adity/Downloads/Analytics%20User%20Guide/output/motor_object/overview_3.dita" xtrc="b:4;35:13">Note</b>: The lower the FSI value the greater the severity of the component fault.</note>
      <p class="- topic/p " xtrf="file:/C:/Users/adity/Downloads/Analytics%20User%20Guide/output/motor_object/overview_3.dita" xtrc="p:2;36:10">For each component in a <b class="+ topic/ph hi-d/b " xtrf="file:/C:/Users/adity/Downloads/Analytics%20User%20Guide/output/motor_object/overview_3.dita" xtrc="b:5;36:37">Warning</b> or an <b class="+ topic/ph hi-d/b " xtrf="file:/C:/Users/adity/Downloads/Analytics%20User%20Guide/output/motor_object/overview_3.dita" xtrc="b:6;36:58">Alarm</b> state, an appropriate <b class="+ topic/ph hi-d/b " xtrf="file:/C:/Users/adity/Downloads/Analytics%20User%20Guide/output/motor_object/overview_3.dita" xtrc="b:7;36:93">Code</b> is assigned by the ADI OtoSense™ Cloud analytics. Each code defines both the recommended Action and the Description of the associated fault.</p>
      <p class="- topic/p " xtrf="file:/C:/Users/adity/Downloads/Analytics%20User%20Guide/output/motor_object/overview_3.dita" xtrc="p:3;37:10">Each component has multiple possible codes depending on the severity of the fault.</p>
      <p class="- topic/p " xtrf="file:/C:/Users/adity/Downloads/Analytics%20User%20Guide/output/motor_object/overview_3.dita" xtrc="p:4;38:10">For example, a Power System component with an FSI of ‘3ʼ or ‘4ʼ will be assigned code ‘1002ʼ and a Power System component with an FSI of ‘2ʼ or below will be assigned code ‘1003ʼ. For more information, see Table 10.</p>
   </conbody>
